{
  "$comment": "HAND-EDITED source of the Settings page layout (SETTINGS-PAGE-FIRST-PRINCIPLES P2, P4): categories by user task in sidebar order, each a list of group cards, plus the action buttons at the end of each section. scripts/cmux-next/gen-settings-sources.py writes the Swift copy (SettingsSchema+PageLayout.generated.swift: SettingsPageLayout and SettingsSchema.actions(in:)); the schema export resolves it into settings-schema.json's `page`, which the web Settings page and the GPUI client draw. A row's key, section and CLI stay as they are; only where the page draws it is decided here. Every row the page shows has exactly one card (SettingsPageLayoutHomeTests). Fields: default_category, the category the page opens on. max_rows_per_card, the most rows one card holds (SettingsPageSectionsTests; user 2026-10-30: \"look a lot better with sections\"). cards, the parts of a category that are not schema rows (id is the export's card id). section_actions, per section id the registry action ids drawn as buttons at the end of that section (titles and availability come from the action registry); every section is listed. sidebar_sections, the sidebar's titled runs of categories (title null for the untitled lead run). A category has id, title ({key, text} or {section: id} for that section's title), symbol (SF Symbol), groups, and optional lead and trail (card ids drawn before and after the groups), actions (sections whose section_actions show at its end), aliases (section ids, from `cmux settings open --section` and old links, that open it), legacy_ids (ids of retired categories, such as mobile and server, whose old #/settings/<id> links open it), dev_only (shown only in DEV builds). A group card has group (a schema group key: its title, and every shown row of that group no other card claims, in schema order), keys (rows claimed by key, drawn after the group's rows), lead_keys (rows claimed by key, drawn first) and title ({key, text}; needed when there is no group). A card with no rows is dropped; a card without a group gets the key <category>.<index>. note is a comment.",
  "default_category": "general",
  "max_rows_per_card": 16,
